{"track":"tahsili","num":"1.01","slug":"algebra-equations","title":"Algebra & Equations","subtitle":"ClipSAT Printable Practice Suite (clipsat.org) • Topic 1.01 • 20 FRQs + 25 MCQs • Difficulty Progression • Cross-Lesson Synthesis","sections":[{"heading":"Part I — Free-Response Questions (FRQs): Foundational Fluency (1–7)","questions":[{"q":"Solve $3x-7=11$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Solving linear equations","answer":"$3x=18$, so $x=6$.","explanation":"$3x=18$, so $x=6$."},{"q":"Solve $5(x-2)=3x+4$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Solving linear equations","answer":"$5x-10=3x+4\\Rightarrow2x=14\\Rightarrow x=7$.","explanation":"$5x-10=3x+4\\Rightarrow2x=14\\Rightarrow x=7$."},{"q":"Solve $\\frac{3x-2}{4}=x-1$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Solving linear equations","answer":"$3x-2=4(x-1)=4x-4\\Rightarrow-x=-2\\Rightarrow x=2$.","explanation":"$3x-2=4(x-1)=4x-4\\Rightarrow-x=-2\\Rightarrow x=2$."},{"q":"Solve $2(x+3)-5=3(x-1)$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Solving linear equations","answer":"$2x+1=3x-3\\Rightarrow-x=-4\\Rightarrow x=4$.","explanation":"$2x+1=3x-3\\Rightarrow-x=-4\\Rightarrow x=4$."},{"q":"Expand and simplify $3(2x-1)-2(x-4)$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Expanding and simplifying expressions","answer":"$6x-3-2x+8=4x+5$.","explanation":"$6x-3-2x+8=4x+5$."},{"q":"Expand $(x+5)(x-2)$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Expanding and simplifying expressions","answer":"$x^2-2x+5x-10=x^2+3x-10$.","explanation":"$x^2-2x+5x-10=x^2+3x-10$."},{"q":"Expand $(2x-3)^2$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Expanding and simplifying expressions","answer":"$(2x-3)^2=4x^2-12x+9$.","explanation":"$(2x-3)^2=4x^2-12x+9$."}]},{"heading":"Part II — Free-Response Questions (FRQs): Intermediate Multi-Step Application (8–14)","questions":[{"q":"Simplify $\\frac{6x^2-9x}{3x}$ (for $x\\neq0$).","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Expanding and simplifying expressions","answer":"$\\frac{3x(2x-3)}{3x}=2x-3$.","explanation":"$\\frac{3x(2x-3)}{3x}=2x-3$."},{"q":"Factor $x^2+7x+12$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Factoring quadratic expressions","answer":"$(x+3)(x+4)$.","explanation":"$(x+3)(x+4)$."},{"q":"Factor $x^2-2x-15$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Factoring quadratic expressions","answer":"$(x-5)(x+3)$.","explanation":"$(x-5)(x+3)$."},{"q":"Factor $2x^2+5x-3$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Factoring quadratic expressions","answer":"$(2x-1)(x+3)$.","explanation":"$(2x-1)(x+3)$."},{"q":"Factor $x^2-49$ using the difference of squares.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Factoring quadratic expressions","answer":"$(x-7)(x+7)$.","explanation":"$(x-7)(x+7)$."},{"q":"Solve $x^2-5x+6=0$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Solving quadratic equations by factoring","answer":"$(x-2)(x-3)=0$, so $x=2$ or $x=3$.","explanation":"$(x-2)(x-3)=0$, so $x=2$ or $x=3$."},{"q":"Solve $x^2+2x-8=0$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Solving quadratic equations by factoring","answer":"$(x+4)(x-2)=0$, so $x=-4$ or $x=2$.","explanation":"$(x+4)(x-2)=0$, so $x=-4$ or $x=2$."}]},{"heading":"Part III — Free-Response Questions (FRQs): Challenging & Cross-Lesson Synthesis (15–20)","questions":[{"q":"Solve $2x^2-5x-3=0$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Solving quadratic equations by factoring","cross_lesson":"8.01 Exponentials & Logarithms","answer":"$(2x+1)(x-3)=0$, so $x=-\\frac{1}{2}$ or $x=3$.","explanation":"$(2x+1)(x-3)=0$, so $x=-\\frac{1}{2}$ or $x=3$."},{"q":"Use the quadratic formula $x=\\frac{-b\\pm\\sqrt{b^2-4ac}}{2a}$ to solve $x^2+3x+1=0$, leaving the answer in exact form.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"FRQ","target":"The quadratic formula and the discriminant","cross_lesson":"9.01 Statistics & Probability","answer":"$a=1,b=3,c=1$. $x=\\frac{-3\\pm\\sqrt{9-4}}{2}=\\frac{-3\\pm\\sqrt{5}}{2}$.","explanation":"$a=1,b=3,c=1$. $x=\\frac{-3\\pm\\sqrt{9-4}}{2}=\\frac{-3\\pm\\sqrt{5}}{2}$."},{"q":"Find the discriminant of $2x^2-4x+5=0$ and state how many real roots it has.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"FRQ","target":"The quadratic formula and the discriminant","cross_lesson":"2.01 Functions & Transformations","answer":"$\\Delta=(-4)^2-4(2)(5)=16-40=-24$. Since $\\Delta<0$, there are no real roots.","explanation":"$\\Delta=(-4)^2-4(2)(5)=16-40=-24$. Since $\\Delta<0$, there are no real roots."},{"q":"Use the quadratic formula to solve $3x^2-2x-1=0$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"FRQ","target":"The quadratic formula and the discriminant","cross_lesson":"3.01 Sequences & Series","answer":"$\\Delta=(-2)^2-4(3)(-1)=4+12=16$. $x=\\frac{2\\pm4}{6}$, so $x=1$ or $x=-\\frac{1}{3}$.","explanation":"$\\Delta=(-2)^2-4(3)(-1)=4+12=16$. $x=\\frac{2\\pm4}{6}$, so $x=1$ or $x=-\\frac{1}{3}$."},{"q":"Solve $|2x+3|=7$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Absolute value equations","cross_lesson":"4.01 Trigonometry","answer":"$2x+3=7\\Rightarrow x=2$, or $2x+3=-7\\Rightarrow x=-5$.","explanation":"$2x+3=7\\Rightarrow x=2$, or $2x+3=-7\\Rightarrow x=-5$."},{"q":"Solve $2x-5<9$ and graph the solution set on a number line.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Linear inequalities","cross_lesson":"5.01 Geometry & Coordinate Geometry","answer":"$2x<14\\Rightarrow x<7$.","explanation":"$2x<14\\Rightarrow x<7$.","figure":{"type":"numberline","min":3,"max":11,"marks":[{"x":7,"open":true,"label":"7"}],"shade":null,"width":250}}]},{"heading":"Part IV — Multiple-Choice Questions (MCQs): Foundational Concept Mastery (21–28)","questions":[{"q":"The graph shows $y=|x-3|$. At what $x$-value does the graph reach its minimum?","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Absolute value equations","choices":["$x=1$","$x=3$","$x=-3$","$x=0$"],"correct":1,"answer":"The vertex of the V-shape (the minimum) is at $x=3$.","explanation":"The vertex of the V-shape (the minimum) is at $x=3$.","figure":{"type":"plot","fns":["abs(x-3)"],"xmin":-1,"xmax":7,"ymin":-1,"ymax":6,"width":230}},{"q":"Solve $3x-7<14$, and identify the graph of its solution set.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Linear inequalities","choices":["$x<7$","$x\\geq7$","$x\\leq7$","$x>7$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$3x<21\\Rightarrow x<7$.","explanation":"$3x<21\\Rightarrow x<7$.","figure":{"type":"numberline","min":2,"max":12,"marks":[{"x":7,"open":true,"label":"$7$"}],"shade":[2,7],"width":250}},{"q":"Solve $-4x+6\\geq-10$, and identify the graph of its solution set.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Linear inequalities","choices":["$x>4$","$x<4$","$x\\leq4$","$x\\geq4$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$-4x\\geq-16$; dividing by $-4$ flips the sign: $x\\leq4$.","explanation":"$-4x\\geq-16$; dividing by $-4$ flips the sign: $x\\leq4$.","figure":{"type":"numberline","min":-1,"max":9,"marks":[{"x":4,"open":false,"label":"$4$"}],"shade":[-1,4],"width":250}},{"q":"The graph shows the system $y=x^2-4$, $y=3x$. What are the points of intersection?","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Linear-quadratic systems","choices":["$(4,12)$ and $(1,3)$","$(-4,-12)$ and $(1,3)$","$(-1,-3)$ and $(1,3)$","$(4,12)$ and $(-1,-3)$"],"correct":3,"answer":"The curve and line cross at $(-1,-3)$ and $(4,12)$.","explanation":"The curve and line cross at $(-1,-3)$ and $(4,12)$.","figure":{"type":"plot","fns":["x**2-4","3*x"],"xmin":-3,"xmax":5,"ymin":-5,"ymax":14,"width":230}},{"q":"The graph shows the system $y=x^2$, $y=2x+3$. What are the points of intersection?","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Linear-quadratic systems","choices":["$(3,9)$ and $(1,1)$","$(-1,1)$ and $(1,1)$","$(-3,9)$ and $(1,1)$","$(3,9)$ and $(-1,1)$"],"correct":3,"answer":"The curve and line cross at $(-1,1)$ and $(3,9)$.","explanation":"The curve and line cross at $(-1,1)$ and $(3,9)$.","figure":{"type":"plot","fns":["x**2","2*x+3"],"xmin":-3,"xmax":4,"ymin":-1,"ymax":10,"width":230}},{"q":"Solve $5x+3=2x-9$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Solving linear equations","choices":["$x=-2$","$x=2$","$x=4$","$x=-4$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$3x=-12\\Rightarrow x=-4$.","explanation":"$3x=-12\\Rightarrow x=-4$."},{"q":"Factor $2x^2-x-6$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Factoring quadratic expressions","choices":["$(2x+3)(x-2)$","$(2x-3)(x+2)$","$(x+3)(2x-2)$","$(2x+1)(x-6)$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$(2x+3)(x-2)=2x^2-4x+3x-6=2x^2-x-6$.","explanation":"$(2x+3)(x-2)=2x^2-4x+3x-6=2x^2-x-6$."},{"q":"Use the quadratic formula to solve $x^2+5x+2=0$, leaving the answer in surd form.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"The quadratic formula and the discriminant","choices":["$x=\\frac{5\\pm\\sqrt{17}}{2}$","$x=\\frac{-5\\pm\\sqrt{17}}{4}$","$x=\\frac{-5\\pm\\sqrt{33}}{2}$","$x=\\frac{-5\\pm\\sqrt{17}}{2}$"],"correct":3,"answer":"Discriminant $=25-8=17$; $x=\\frac{-5\\pm\\sqrt{17}}{2}$.","explanation":"Discriminant $=25-8=17$; $x=\\frac{-5\\pm\\sqrt{17}}{2}$."}]},{"heading":"Part V — Multiple-Choice Questions (MCQs): Intermediate Exam Application (29–37)","questions":[{"q":"Use the quadratic formula to solve $2x^2+3x-2=0$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"The quadratic formula and the discriminant","choices":["$x=1$ or $x=-2$","$x=-0.5$ or $x=2$","$x=0.5$ or $x=-2$","$x=0.5$ or $x=2$"],"correct":2,"answer":"Discriminant $=9+16=25$; $x=\\frac{-3\\pm5}{4}$: $x=0.5$ or $x=-2$.","explanation":"Discriminant $=9+16=25$; $x=\\frac{-3\\pm5}{4}$: $x=0.5$ or $x=-2$."},{"q":"Solve $2x+5>-3$ and $x-1<6$ together (both must hold). Find the combined solution set.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Linear inequalities","choices":["$x>-4$","$-4<x\\leq7$","$x<7$","$-4<x<7$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$2x+5>-3\\Rightarrow x>-4$; $x-1<6\\Rightarrow x<7$. Together: $-4<x<7$.","explanation":"$2x+5>-3\\Rightarrow x>-4$; $x-1<6\\Rightarrow x<7$. Together: $-4<x<7$."},{"q":"The sum of two numbers is $22$ and their difference is $6$. Find the two numbers.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Systems of linear equations","choices":["$11$ and $11$","$14$ and $6$","$16$ and $6$","$14$ and $8$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$x+y=22$, $x-y=6\\Rightarrow x=14$, $y=8$.","explanation":"$x+y=22$, $x-y=6\\Rightarrow x=14$, $y=8$."},{"q":"Solve the system $2x-y=7$, $3x+2y=21$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Systems of linear equations","choices":["$x=5$, $y=-3$","$x=5$, $y=3$","$x=3$, $y=5$","$x=7$, $y=7$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$y=2x-7\\Rightarrow3x+2(2x-7)=21\\Rightarrow7x=35\\Rightarrow x=5$; $y=3$.","explanation":"$y=2x-7\\Rightarrow3x+2(2x-7)=21\\Rightarrow7x=35\\Rightarrow x=5$; $y=3$."},{"q":"Solve $\\frac{4}{x-1}=\\frac{2}{x+2}$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Rational equations","choices":["$x=-5$","$x=5$","$x=-1$","$x=2$"],"correct":0,"answer":"Cross-multiply: $4(x+2)=2(x-1)\\Rightarrow4x+8=2x-2\\Rightarrow x=-5$.","explanation":"Cross-multiply: $4(x+2)=2(x-1)\\Rightarrow4x+8=2x-2\\Rightarrow x=-5$."},{"q":"Solve $\\frac{6}{x}=\\frac{2}{x-4}$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Rational equations","choices":["$x=12$","$x=4$","$x=-6$","$x=6$"],"correct":3,"answer":"Cross-multiply: $6(x-4)=2x\\Rightarrow6x-24=2x\\Rightarrow x=6$.","explanation":"Cross-multiply: $6(x-4)=2x\\Rightarrow6x-24=2x\\Rightarrow x=6$."},{"q":"The perimeter of a rectangle is $P=2l+2w$. Solve for $l$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Solving for a variable in a formula","choices":["$l=\\frac{P}{2}-w$","$l=\\frac{P-2w}{2}$","$l=\\frac{P+2w}{2}$","$l=P-2w$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$P-2w=2l\\Rightarrow l=\\frac{P-2w}{2}$ (equivalently $\\frac{P}{2}-w$).","explanation":"$P-2w=2l\\Rightarrow l=\\frac{P-2w}{2}$ (equivalently $\\frac{P}{2}-w$)."},{"q":"The formula for simple interest is $I=Prt$. Solve for $r$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Solving for a variable in a formula","choices":["$r=\\frac{I}{P}$","$r=\\frac{I}{Pt}$","$r=\\frac{Pt}{I}$","$r=I-Pt$"],"correct":1,"answer":"Dividing both sides by $Pt$: $r=\\frac{I}{Pt}$.","explanation":"Dividing both sides by $Pt$: $r=\\frac{I}{Pt}$."},{"q":"The formula $F=\\frac{9}{5}C+32$ converts Celsius to Fahrenheit. Solve for $C$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Solving for a variable in a formula","choices":["$C=\\frac{5(F-32)}{9}$","$C=\\frac{5F-32}{9}$","$C=\\frac{5}{9}F+32$","$C=\\frac{9(F-32)}{5}$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$F-32=\\frac{9}{5}C\\Rightarrow C=\\frac{5(F-32)}{9}$.","explanation":"$F-32=\\frac{9}{5}C\\Rightarrow C=\\frac{5(F-32)}{9}$."}]},{"heading":"Part VI — Multiple-Choice Questions (MCQs): Challenging & Cross-Lesson Synthesis (38–45)","questions":[{"q":"The volume of a cylinder is $V=\\pi r^2h$. Solve for $h$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Solving for a variable in a formula","choices":["$h=\\frac{V}{\\pi r^2}$","$h=V-\\pi r^2$","$h=\\frac{V}{\\pi r}$","$h=\\frac{\\pi r^2}{V}$"],"correct":0,"answer":"Dividing both sides by $\\pi r^2$: $h=\\frac{V}{\\pi r^2}$.","explanation":"Dividing both sides by $\\pi r^2$: $h=\\frac{V}{\\pi r^2}$.","cross_lesson":"3.01 Sequences & Series"},{"q":"Solve the system $y=x^2-4$, $y=3x$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Linear-quadratic systems","choices":["$(-4,-12)$ and $(1,3)$","$(-1,-3)$ and $(1,3)$","$(4,12)$ and $(1,3)$","$(4,12)$ and $(-1,-3)$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$x^2-4=3x\\Rightarrow x^2-3x-4=0\\Rightarrow(x-4)(x+1)=0$: $x=4,y=12$ or $x=-1,y=-3$.","explanation":"$x^2-4=3x\\Rightarrow x^2-3x-4=0\\Rightarrow(x-4)(x+1)=0$: $x=4,y=12$ or $x=-1,y=-3$.","cross_lesson":"4.01 Trigonometry"},{"q":"Solve the system $y=x^2$, $y=2x+3$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Linear-quadratic systems","choices":["$(-3,9)$ and $(1,1)$","$(3,9)$ and $(1,1)$","$(-1,1)$ and $(1,1)$","$(3,9)$ and $(-1,1)$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$x^2-2x-3=0\\Rightarrow(x-3)(x+1)=0$: $x=3,y=9$ or $x=-1,y=1$.","explanation":"$x^2-2x-3=0\\Rightarrow(x-3)(x+1)=0$: $x=3,y=9$ or $x=-1,y=1$.","cross_lesson":"5.01 Geometry & Coordinate Geometry"},{"q":"A rectangular garden has a length that is 5 meters more than its width, and its area is 84 square meters. Find the width.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Word problems: setting up and solving equations","choices":["$12$","$7$","$9$","$14$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$w(w+5)=84\\Rightarrow(w+12)(w-7)=0$; the positive root is $w=7$.","explanation":"$w(w+5)=84\\Rightarrow(w+12)(w-7)=0$; the positive root is $w=7$.","cross_lesson":"6.01 Limits & Derivatives"},{"q":"A mobile-data plan charges a fixed monthly fee of 40 riyals plus 2 riyals per GB used. If a user's bill was 68 riyals, how many GB did they use?","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Word problems: setting up and solving equations","choices":["$34$","$14$","$54$","$28$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$40+2g=68\\Rightarrow2g=28\\Rightarrow g=14$.","explanation":"$40+2g=68\\Rightarrow2g=28\\Rightarrow g=14$.","cross_lesson":"7.01 Integration & Applications"},{"q":"Solve $4(x-1)=x+11$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Algebra & Equations","choices":["$-5$","$3$","$5$","$7$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$4x-4=x+11\\Rightarrow 3x=15\\Rightarrow x=5$.","explanation":"$4x-4=x+11\\Rightarrow 3x=15\\Rightarrow x=5$.","cross_lesson":"8.01 Exponentials & Logarithms"},{"q":"Solve $4(x+9)=x+36$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Algebra & Equations","choices":["$3$","$-2$","$0$","$2$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$4x+36=x+36\\Rightarrow 3x=0\\Rightarrow x=0$.","explanation":"$4x+36=x+36\\Rightarrow 3x=0\\Rightarrow x=0$.","cross_lesson":"9.01 Statistics & Probability"},{"q":"Solve $4(x-1)=2x-8$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Algebra & Equations","choices":["$2$","$0$","$-4$","$-2$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$4x-4=2x-8\\Rightarrow 2x=-4\\Rightarrow x=-2$.","explanation":"$4x-4=2x-8\\Rightarrow 2x=-4\\Rightarrow x=-2$.","cross_lesson":"2.01 Functions & Transformations"}]}]}